\par SCRL\tab The Scroll Lock key is latched down.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f9 \page }{\cs15\fs16\up6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f8\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs15\fs16\up6 #}{ HID_WINDOW_NEW}}}{\b\f9 
New command (Window menu)}{\f9 
\par 
\par Use this command to open a new window with the same contents as the active window.  You can open multiple document windows to display different parts or views of a document at t
he same time.  If you change the contents in one window, all other windows containing the same document reflect those changes.  When you open a new window, it becomes the active window and is displayed on top of all other open windows.
\par 
\par \page }{\cs15\fs16\up6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f8\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs15\fs16\up6 #}{ HID_WINDOW_CASCADE}}}{\b\f9 Cascade command (Window menu)}{\f9 
\par 
\par Use this command to arrange multiple opened windows in an overlapped fashion. 
\par 
\par \page }{\cs15\fs16\up6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f8\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs15\fs16\up6 #}{ HID_WINDOW_TILE}}}{\b\f9 Tile command (Window menu)}{\f9 
\par 
\par Use this command to arrange multiple opened windows in a non-overlapped fashion.
\par 
\par 
\par \page }{\cs15\fs16\up6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f8\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs15\fs16\up6 #}{ HID_WINDOW_TILE_HORZ}}}{\b\f9 Tile Horizontal command (Window menu)}{\f9 
\par 
\par Use this command to vertically arrange multiple opened windows in a non-overlapped fashion.
\par \page }{\cs15\fs16\up6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f8\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs15\fs16\up6 #}{ HID_WINDOW_TILE_VERT}}}{\b\f9 Tile Vertical command (Window menu)}{\f9 
\par 
\par Use this command to arrange multiple opened windows side by side.
\par \page }{\cs15\fs16\up6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f8\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs15\fs16\up6 #}{ HID_WINDOW_ARRANGE}}}{\b\f9 Window Arrange Icons Command}{\f9 
\par 
\par Use this command to arrange the icons for minimized windows at the bottom of the main window.  If there is an open document window at the bottom of the main window, then some or 
all of the icons may not be visible because they will be underneath this document window.\page }{\cs15\fs16\up6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f8\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
