\par 
\par }{\f9 Use this command to split the active window into panes.  You may then use the mouse or the keyboard arrows to move th
e splitter bars.  When you are finished, press the mouse button or enter to leave the splitter bars in their new location.  Pressing escape keeps the splitter bars in their original location.  << In a single document interface application, this command wi
ll appear on the View menu. >>\page }{\cs15\fs16\up6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f8\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs15\fs16\up6 #}{ HID_WINDOW_ALL}}}{\b\f9 
1, 2, ... command (Window menu)}{\f9 
\par 
\par <<YourApp>> displays a list of currently open document windows at the bottom of the Window menu.  A check mark appears in front of the document name of the active window.  Choose a document from this list to make its window active.  
\par \page }{\cs15\fs16\up6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f8\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs15\fs16\up6 #}{ HID_HELP_INDEX}}}{\b\f9 Index command (Help menu)
